cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kessler: collision-risk monitoring for small satellites"
authors:
  - family-names: Vazquez
    given-names: Nicolas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4300-6369"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickvaz09/kessler"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23448061
license: MIT
keywords:
  - space debris
  - collision avoidance
  - conjunction assessment
  - machine learning
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Kessler screens the public satellite catalog for close approaches with SGP4,
  forecasts collision risk with VIGIL, a model trained on ESA's Collision
  Avoidance Challenge data, and re-evaluates that model in four pre-registered
  rounds (the VIGIL Lab).
